Trafficmancy was a project put together for the 2024 LCC Technicians Exhibition. 

Tech-wise, the responses you're getting are coming from the Ollama dolphin-phi model that is running entirely on the Nvidia Jetson. The information about bikes, the tube, etc is being retrieved using the TFL API. The interface was made with a Python library called pyxel, which is meant to be the Python equivalent of "fantasy consoles" like the TIC-80.

The idea came from a Rosicrucian dude I used to know who could hear voices, and who told me he could make predictions from the future using absolutely anything...

I find it neat that LLMs can easily find the "product" of different ideas.